    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "DEC-15 — the design-run enforcement model: a run is a fifth governed artifact checked on every write; the receipt covers soft rules only, because a rule with a Tier-1 predicate is judged by the predicate and a hand verdict on a machine-checkable rule is the row that can be wrong for free; coverage is read from the rulebook on disk so a rule change re-opens every receipt; the unimplemented gap is printed rather than filed; and the gate proves a receipt complete and well-formed, never true. Three consequences added or corrected in later rounds: the archived-run model and why the newest run and any open run are never archived; a run's own failures are the check inventory, which is the model working rather than a sign it was under-specified; and a predicate's vocabulary is closed — the artifact is the suspect when a new check reds, because a gate that bends converts an open defect into a green receipt"
